  "limitations": [
    "Passive, observational workload; outputs, tool loops, auxiliary calls, context sizes and settings differ. No cross-model speed or quality ranking is established.",
    "The ten controlled requests precede the full restart: four include prefix preparation, six measure already prepared reuse. They are not ten post-restart SSD-return tests.",
    "Controlled preparation can occur before the final native request. A high cached count in that final request does not remove preparation cost from client wall time.",
    "Laptop first-request API latency includes lazy loading. No separately timed post-load TTFT, isolated reload duration or native generation TPS is available; missing values remain null.",
    "A full Hermes turn can contain multiple API calls and tool execution. Per-call latency is not whole-task duration.",
    "Desktop native first token, proxy first byte and controlled first nonempty SSE token are different clocks. Proxy framing can precede a native text token.",
    "Completed rows only; cancellation, unmatched lifecycle completions and in-progress requests are disclosed separately.",
    "Partial histories and new suffixes still require computation. Large new suffixes and the long-tail request remain in the published data.",
    "The desktop native log records one later partially-ready state. The snapshot does not diagnose its cause or prove both bases stayed ready continuously.",
    "No new inference, warmup, restart or Telegram message was sent to collect these observations."
  ],
